IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc19-s492-26`

-- ccc19-tests-s492-26.l4 -- tests for ccc19-s492-26.l4 (Criminal Code (Canada) s 492.26, Case Complexity).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the subsection named beside it, before the run. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `s 492.26(1) -- In determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall consider whether there are any relevant factors ... making the case complex`

#ASSERT `s 492.26(1) the court must consider whether any relevant factors contributed or will contribute to making the case complex` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in the course of that determination: nothing owed under this subsection
#ASSERT `s 492.26(1) the court must consider whether any relevant factors contributed or will contribute to making the case complex` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Determining, nothing done yet: the standing obligation (the text gives no period).
#TRACE `s 492.26(1) the duty of the court to consider case complexity` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- Determining, the court considers: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 492.26(1) the duty of the court to consider case complexity` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.26(1) consider whether there are any relevant factors that contributed or will contribute to making the case complex` AT 1

-- Not determining: nothing owed.
#TRACE `s 492.26(1) the duty of the court to consider case complexity` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§ `s 492.26(2) -- If the case involved or will involve applications or motions, the court shall also consider the following factors`

-- Each of the seven named factors, (a) to (g), when the case involved applications or motions: the court must consider it (the court's own finding of relevance is not asked for (a) to (g))
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(a) the number of applications or motions` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(b) whether any of the applications or motions required or will require scheduling court dates separately and in advance of trial dates` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(d) whether more than one judicial decision was or will be needed to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(e) the amount of cumulative court time that was or will be required to adjudicate the applications or motions` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(f) the need for trial continuation dates arising from the applications or motions that required more time than anticipated` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(g) the need for trial continuation dates arising from the applications or motions that were not scheduled in advance of the trial` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paragraph (h): any factor the court finds relevant in assessing the complexity of the applications or motions
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(h) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (g)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- another factor that the court does not find relevant: the list is not closed with "only", so not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(h) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (g)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the case did not and will not involve applications or motions: the "If" is not met, so no duty under this subsection, whatever the factor
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` FALSE `s 492.26(2)(a) the number of applications or motions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.26(2) the court must also consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` FALSE `s 492.26(2)(h) another factor, not named in paragraphs (a) to (g)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The regulative rule, for factor (c): the standing obligation; performed for (c): FULFILLED; the court considers only (a): the guard rejects it and the duty for (c) stands.
#TRACE `s 492.26(2) the duty of the court to consider the factor` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

#TRACE `s 492.26(2) the duty of the court to consider the factor` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.26(2) consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` `s 492.26(2)(c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions` AT 2

#TRACE `s 492.26(2) the duty of the court to consider the factor` TRUE `s 492.26(2)(c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.26(2) consider the factor in assessing whether the case is complex` `s 492.26(2)(a) the number of applications or motions` AT 2

-- No applications or motions: nothing owed.
#TRACE `s 492.26(2) the duty of the court to consider the factor` FALSE `s 492.26(2)(c) whether any adjournments were or will be required in order to complete the steps required by any of the applications or motions` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)
